 SecFn does not re-export Express, Hono, Fastify, Next.js, or SvelteKit adapters. Mount the returned router with the existing shared HTTP adapter packages.
+
+## Security defaults
+
+- **Admin routes fail closed.** Every `/admin/*` route requires the `authorize`
+  callback to return `true`. If `authorize` is omitted the route is denied and a
+  `permission_denied` audit event is written. Deployments that enforce
+  authorization upstream (e.g. at an API gateway) and intentionally mount the
+  routes unprotected must opt in with `unsafeAllowUnauthenticatedAdmin: true`.
